From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-bandix-plus: phone layout, WAN direction, ranking
 over all interfaces, Russian translation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On screens up to 768 px the status page left the device table to the
theme, which stacked every cell of a row on its own line without
labels; the usage ranking items overlapped; the query panels took most
of a screen each. Rates in the interface cards were cut to "2.8..." on
the desktop too, and the device table cut the MAC and IPv4 columns.

Now:

- interface cards keep the whole rate and volume (they wrap instead of
  being cut) and are titled Upload / Download like the device list
  ("Inbound" / "Outbound" before); the zone badge and the "(zone)"
  suffix in the interface selects are shown only when the zone is known
  (not "unknown");
- the counters of an interface are ingress and egress: on a LAN
  interface ingress is what devices upload, on a WAN interface it is
  what is downloaded from outside. For interfaces in a firewall zone
  named wan* the card, the realtime chart and the traffic timeline swap
  the two directions, so Upload and Download mean the same on every
  card (a WAN interface in the list then shows the total internet
  traffic);
- the desktop device table sizes its columns by content and scrolls
  sideways when it does not fit;
- on narrow screens the device list is a list of cards: the name (or
  the address), the interface and the address, the upload and download
  rate with the volume for the period under it; detailed mode adds the
  MAC, extra IPv4, IPv6 and the last seen time; offline devices are
  dimmed. A Sort select (address, rate, volume, name, interface) is
  shown above the cards; the desktop table keeps sorting by its
  headers;
- filters show the label and the select in one row; date fields, the
  Query/Reset buttons and the period presets use two columns; ranking
  items keep the rank, the name and the volumes in one block; the
  timeline totals are three columns;
- the usage ranking has "All interfaces" (default): one request per
  monitored interface, merged and sorted by volume; every item shows its
  interface;
- the hostname "-" from the API is replaced by the address in the
  ranking and in the device selects; the chart point counter reads
  "Points: N";
- status.css is requested with a new version so that browsers do not
  keep the old file.

The Russian translation is rewritten for the strings that remain on
the pages: upload and download were both translated as "загрузка",
Reset as "перезагрузить", and some strings were machine-translated
out of context.

